<article class="env-exercise" id="0CVS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CVS">Exercise <span data-tag="0CVS">111.21.2</span>.</a> Let $k$ be your favorite algebraically closed field. Let $n \geq 1$. Let $k[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]$ be the polynomial ring. Set $\mathfrak m = (x_1, \ldots , x_ n)$. Let $k[x_1, \ldots , x_ n] \subset A$ be a finite type extension of domains. Set $d = \dim (A)$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that $d - 1 \geq \dim (A/\mathfrak m A) \geq d - n$ if $A/\mathfrak mA \not= 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show by example that every value can occur. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show by example that $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A/\mathfrak m A)$ can have irreducible components of different dimensions. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>